      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Alterations in normal breath sounds are an important indication of pathophysiological processes in the bronchial system and the lung. In the presence of non-specific symptoms like dyspnea, wheezing or cough while sleeping it seems reasonable to make a nocturnal long-term recording of breath sounds. Thus specific auscultation phenomena can be recorded qualitative and particularly quantitative in the course. A mobile recording system provides a non-invasive monitoring at home which is independent of vigilance. Furthermore it can be used for follow-up examinations of medical interventions."},
